{
  "company_name": "MidLedger Analytics",
  "industry": "Oil & Gas Midstream",
  "use_case": "Financial analytics and reporting for oil & gas midstream operations",
  "space_title": "MidLedger Analytics - Financial Analytics & Reporting 💰",
  "space_description": "**Subindustry:** Oil & Gas Midstream\n\n**Use case:** Financial Analytics & Reporting\n\nMidLedger Analytics — financial performance analytics across midstream divisions, cost centers, and operating regions. The CFO and FP&A leadership use this space to track operating margin, ROIC, and EBITDA against plan; division presidents use it to manage budget variance and headcount-adjusted unit economics.\n\n**Key KPIs**\n- EBITDA ($) — primary profitability metric\n- Operating margin (%) — current portfolio ranges -10% to 35%; healthy divisions trend above 20%\n- ROIC (%) — return on invested capital (target >WACC, typically 8-10%)\n- Revenue actual vs. plan ($) — top-line variance\n- OpEx actual vs. plan ($) — cost-side variance\n- Cost per unit ($) — unit economics across cost centers\n- Headcount — labor capacity by division\n- Budget variance (%) — actual vs. budget at GL-category level\n\n**Data sources**\n- `financial_transactions` — individual GL entries with budget comparison\n- `budget_snapshots` — periodic actual vs. plan revenue, opex, EBITDA\n- `financial_kpi_monthly` — monthly operating margin, ROIC, cost-per-unit",
  "schema_basename": "og_midstream_finance",
  "tables": [
    {
      "table_name": "financial_transactions",
